<h2>During-Storm Strategies: Capturing the Surge</h2>

<p>
When a severe storm hits your market, you have 24 to 72 hours to capture the majority of leads. Every hour of delay costs you jobs. This section covers the exact actions to take from the moment a storm is confirmed.
</p>

<h3>Activate Emergency PPC Campaigns</h3>

<p>
Google Ads is the fastest way to reach storm-damaged homeowners. Within 30 minutes of a storm, homeowners are searching "roof repair after hail," "emergency roof tarping," and "roofing contractor near me." Your ads need to be live before they finish typing.
</p>

<p>
Set up emergency campaign templates in your Google Ads account before storm season. When a storm hits, duplicate the template, update the location targeting to the affected zip codes, and activate. Your campaigns should include:
</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Emergency keywords:</strong> "emergency roof repair," "roof tarping," "storm damage roof," "hail damage repair," "wind damage roof," "tree fell on roof," plus city and zip code modifiers.</li>
<li><strong>Negative keywords:</strong> "DIY," "how to," "cost to," "cheap," "self" — filter out researchers and keep your budget focused on buyers.</li>
<li><strong>Ad copy:</strong> Lead with urgency. "24/7 Emergency Roof Repair in [City]. Free Inspection. We Bill Insurance. Call Now." Include call extensions, location extensions, and sitelinks to your storm landing page.</li>
<li><strong>Budget:</strong> Set daily budgets 5x to 10x your normal spend. Storm traffic is concentrated and temporary. A $200 daily budget becomes $1,000 to $2,000 for 48 to 72 hours.</li>
</ul>

